# an ordinary commit payload, the shape every session sends dozens of times. Not a tracker write, so the hook reports nothing — and runs nothing. #305 found the hook executing the backtick spans of its own comments on exactly this payload: a header comment carried real control characters where the two-character escapes for newline, tab and return were meant, and the line after the break began with a bare backtick outside any comment. tools/verify-hook-source.sh is the gate that catches that shape; this case is the payload it was found on
{"tool_name":"Bash","cwd":"__FIXTURE_MAIN__","tool_input":{"command":"git commit -m x"}}
